<h2>What this site is</h2>
<p>neocloud.fyi is a set of static pages: a source-linked evidence corpus about GPU neoclouds
and the knowledge needed to run one. It is a work in progress. There is no account, no form,
no comment box and no database of visitors.</p>

<h2>Cookies, analytics and third parties</h2>
<ul>
  <li>No cookies. The site sets none and reads none.</li>
  <li>No analytics, no tracking scripts, no advertising, no social-media buttons.</li>
  <li>No third-party requests. Pages load no script, font, image or frame from another
  origin; the typefaces are served from this site. Links to the companies' own pages are
  ordinary links and send nothing until you click them.</li>
  <li>Nothing is stored in your browser. The light or dark colour scheme follows your system
  setting and is not saved.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Who hosts it</h2>
<p>The site is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. Cloudflare delivers and protects the site, and like
any host it handles technical request data such as your IP address and the pages you ask for.
That processing is Cloudflare's; see
<a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
I do not run analytics on top of it and I do not look at who visited.</p>

<h2>Email to the corrections address</h2>
<p>The one way to contact this site is email to
<a href="mailto:corrections@neocloud.fyi">corrections@neocloud.fyi</a>. If you write, I get your
email address and whatever you put in the message.</p>
<ul>
  <li>I use it to check the correction against its source and to reply to you. Nothing else:
  no mailing list, no marketing, no sharing.</li>
  <li>I name you in the changelog only if you ask me to.</li>
  <li>I keep the message while the correction is open and for as long afterwards as I need to
  show why a row changed, then delete it.</li>
  <li>My basis for this is legitimate interest in keeping the record accurate (UK GDPR). You
  can ask to see, correct or delete your message by writing to the same address, and you
  can complain to the <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">Information
  Commissioner's Office</a>.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Who is responsible</h2>
<p>Joan Marc Riera Duocastella, United Kingdom, is the controller of anything described
above. Contact: <a href="mailto:corrections@neocloud.fyi">corrections@neocloud.fyi</a>.</p>

<h2>Data, sources and licences</h2>
<p>The facts on the site are public facts with a source link and a checked date each. How
they are compiled, and what the licences are, is on the <a href="/sources/">sources page</a>.</p>
